-- title:
--   Core function fields, places, reduction data, and Frobenius objects
-- statement:
--   This interface fixes the algebraic closure $\overline{ℚ}$, the subgroup $Γ_H(25)$, the rational and geometric modular function fields, their versions over an arbitrary coefficient field, and the corresponding place types. It defines rational geometric places, the constant-field embedding, the modular $j$-function, residue-field specializations, reduction and Frobenius maps, the Frobenius-fixed Picard subgroup and its fixed-point equivalence, and a carrier for cusp choices. These objects form the common vocabulary for good reduction, place counts, cuspidal divisors, and the final Kummer argument.
-- source:
--   B. Mazur, Modular curves and the Eisenstein ideal, Publ. IHES 47 (1977); Lean formalization of the order-25 case for this mission. Modules in the MazurProof/Keystone/Tate families are adapted from anthropics/fermats-last-theorem (Apache-2.0) via the xiangyazi24/FLT fork.

