/-! ### The `j`-invariant as a ratio of integral forms

`jBase25` needs that the `q`-expansion of `j` lies in the field generated by ratios of
integral weight-12 forms of every level. The proof writes `j = E₄³ / Δ` and identifies the
`q`-expansion of the discriminant with `X · η²⁴`; it is proved here because the definition
of `jBase25` depends on it. -/

